The goal is to identify DNA damage that is found at higher levels or remains in the oral cells longer because they might be more important in causing cancer than other types of DNA damage.","timeFrame":"DNA damage will be assessed at baseline and Days 3, 6, 12, and 21 after stopping use or continuing use"},{"measure":"Urinary smoking markers","description":"Total nicotine equivalents (TNE), cyanoethyl mercapturic acid (CEMA), and NNAL will be measured in the urine of participants to confirm if they smoked during the study. The concentration of these compounds will be reported at pmol/mL urine","timeFrame":"Urine levels will be measured at baseline and Days 3, 6, 12, and 21 after stopping use or continuing use."}],"secondaryOutcomes":[{"measure":"Urinary vape markers","description":"Propylene glycol and glycerol will be measured in the urine of participants to confirm if they vaped during the study. The concentration of these compounds will be reported as pmol/mL urine.","timeFrame":"Vaping markers will be measured in the urine at baseline and Days 3, 6, 12 and 21 after stopping or continuing use."}]},"eligibilityModule":{"eligibilityCriteria":"Inclusion Criteria:

